Chapter: TestDiskCompileScript

  cites Foreword chapter Console
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe
  cites Shell chapter ShellTypes
  cites Shell chapter ShellBuild
  cites Shell chapter Pipeline
  cites Shell chapter PowerShellEmit

 We say:

Section: Parameters

 The sample has to be CITE-FREE. The image plug embeds it raw and the compiler
 reads it from the disk inside the VM, so nothing resolves a cites line on the
 way in; a sample with one compiles on the host in step 1a and then fails in
 step 2 for a reason the output does not name.

 An EMPTY DiskPath means "whatever name the sample lands under", derived below
 from SampleSrc. The default was the literal SOURCE.SRC while the img plug
 spelled every source's name that way; since the plug gives each source its own
 8.3 name, a second literal here would name a file the image no longer holds,
 and would do it the moment anybody changed SampleSrc.

  tdc-params : List ShellParam = [sh-param-default "DiskPath" SptString (SeLit ""), sh-param-default "SampleSrc" SptString (SeLit "codex\\test\\field-range-proven.codex"), sh-param-default "Expected" SptString (SeLit "12"), sh-param-default "PCore" SptInt (SeInt 1)]

Section: S01 -- Preamble

  s01-body : List ShellCmd = [ScSetStrictMode, ScSetErrorStop, ScBlank, ScRunDot (SeRaw "(Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'vm-config.ps1')"), ScBlank, ScRaw "# The 8.3 name codex/plugs/img/run.ps1 folds a source to, so this test names", ScRaw "# the file the image actually carries whatever SampleSrc is.", ScRaw "if (-not $DiskPath) {", ScRaw "    $n83 = ([System.IO.Path]::GetFileNameWithoutExtension($SampleSrc)).ToUpperInvariant() -replace '[^A-Z0-9_\\-]', '_'", ScRaw "    $e83 = ([System.IO.Path]::GetExtension($SampleSrc).TrimStart('.')).ToUpperInvariant() -replace '[^A-Z0-9_\\-]', '_'", ScRaw "    if ($n83.Length -gt 8) { $n83 = $n83.Substring(0, 8) }", ScRaw "    if ($e83.Length -gt 3) { $e83 = $e83.Substring(0, 3) }", ScRaw "    $DiskPath = if ($e83) { \"$n83.$e83\" } else { $n83 }", ScRaw "}", ScBlank, ScAssign "root" (SeRaw "Split-Path $PSScriptRoot"), ScAssign "outDir" (SeRaw "Join-Path $root 'build-output\\disk-compile-test'"), ScIf (SeNot (SeDirExists (SeVar "outDir"))) [ScMkdir (SeVar "outDir")] [], ScAssign "compile" (SeRaw "Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'compile.ps1'"), ScAssign "runScript" (SeRaw "Join-Path $PSScriptRoot 'test-run.ps1'"), ScEchoStyled (SeLit "=== DISK compile test ===") ClBrightCyan True]

Section: S01b -- FAT16 extraction helper

 DISK mode does not stream the compiled binary. `emit-binary-tail` prints the
 SIZE: line and then writes OUT.CDX to the volume, so the artifact comes back
 on the disk image and not on the wire, and the host reads it after the VM is
 closed.

 FAT16 is not our format, so the offsets are the spec's: BPB bytes-per-sector
 at 11, sectors-per-cluster at 13, reserved at 14, FAT count at 16, root
 entries at 17, sectors-per-FAT at 22, and the 0x55AA signature at 510. A
 directory entry is 32 bytes, first byte 0xE5 meaning deleted and attribute
 0x0F at offset 11 meaning a long-name fragment; cluster is at 26 and size at
 28. A chain ends at or above 0xFFF8. The partition is at LBA 2048, which the
 signature check refuses loudly rather than guessing at.

  s01b-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScRaw "function Read-Exact {\n    param($Stream, [byte[]]$Buffer, [int]$Offset, [int]$Length)\n    $n = 0\n    while ($n -lt $Length) {\n        $r = $Stream.Read($Buffer, ($Offset + $n), ($Length - $n))\n        if ($r -le 0) { break }\n        $n += $r\n    }\n    return $n\n}\n\n\nfunction Export-Fat16File {\n    param([string]$Image, [string]$Name, [string]$Out)\n    # Stop-VmGraceful's Stop-Process returns before the guest's handles are\n    # gone, so a plain OpenRead here loses a race that reads on the verdict\n    # line exactly like a DISK-mode failure. Retry, then say which it was.\n    $fs = $null\n    for ($try = 0; ($try -lt 40) -and ($null -eq $fs); $try++) {\n        try { $fs = [System.IO.File]::OpenRead($Image) } catch { Start-Sleep -Milliseconds 250 }\n    }\n    if ($null -eq $fs) { throw \"FAT16: $Image was still held 10s after the VM closed; the guest did not release it\" }\n    try {\n        $bpb = New-Object byte[] 512\n        $fs.Seek((2048 * 512), 'Begin') | Out-Null\n        if ((Read-Exact -Stream $fs -Buffer $bpb -Offset 0 -Length 512) -ne 512) { throw 'FAT16: cannot read the BPB at LBA 2048' }\n        if (($bpb[510] -ne 85) -or ($bpb[511] -ne 170)) { throw 'FAT16: no boot signature at LBA 2048' }\n        $bps = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($bpb, 11)\n        $spc = $bpb[13]\n        $rsvd = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($bpb, 14)\n        $nfat = $bpb[16]\n        $rent = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($bpb, 17)\n        $spf = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($bpb, 22)\n        if (($bps -le 0) -or ($spc -le 0) -or ($spf -le 0) -or ($nfat -le 0)) { throw \"FAT16: implausible BPB bps=$bps spc=$spc spf=$spf nfat=$nfat\" }\n        $fatSec = 2048 + $rsvd\n        $rootSec = $fatSec + ($nfat * $spf)\n        $rootSecs = [int][Math]::Ceiling(($rent * 32) / $bps)\n        $dataSec = $rootSec + $rootSecs\n        $rd = New-Object byte[] ($rootSecs * $bps)\n        $fs.Seek(($rootSec * $bps), 'Begin') | Out-Null\n        if ((Read-Exact -Stream $fs -Buffer $rd -Offset 0 -Length $rd.Length) -ne $rd.Length) { throw 'FAT16: short read of the root directory' }\n        $clus = 0\n        $size = 0\n        for ($e = 0; $e -lt $rent; $e++) {\n            $o = $e * 32\n            if ($rd[$o] -eq 0) { break }\n            if (($rd[$o] -eq 229) -or ($rd[$o + 11] -eq 15)) { continue }\n            if ([System.Text.Encoding]::ASCII.GetString($rd, $o, 11) -eq $Name) {\n                $clus = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($rd, $o + 26)\n                $size = [BitConverter]::ToUInt32($rd, $o + 28)\n                break\n            }\n        }\n        if ($clus -lt 2) { throw \"FAT16: $Name is not in the root directory\" }\n        $fat = New-Object byte[] ($spf * $bps)\n        $fs.Seek(($fatSec * $bps), 'Begin') | Out-Null\n        if ((Read-Exact -Stream $fs -Buffer $fat -Offset 0 -Length $fat.Length) -ne $fat.Length) { throw 'FAT16: short read of the FAT' }\n        $bytes = New-Object byte[] $size\n        $got = 0\n        $cl = $clus\n        while ((($got -lt $size) -and ($cl -ge 2)) -and ($cl -lt 65528)) {\n            $take = [Math]::Min(($spc * $bps), ($size - $got))\n            $fs.Seek((($dataSec + ($cl - 2) * $spc) * $bps), 'Begin') | Out-Null\n            if ((Read-Exact -Stream $fs -Buffer $bytes -Offset $got -Length $take) -ne $take) { throw \"FAT16: short read in $Name at cluster $cl\" }\n            $got += $take\n            $cl = [BitConverter]::ToUInt16($fat, $cl * 2)\n        }\n        if ($got -ne $size) { throw \"FAT16: $Name chain yielded $got of $size bytes\" }\n        [System.IO.File]::WriteAllBytes($Out, $bytes)\n        return $size\n    } finally {\n        $fs.Close()\n    }\n}"]

Section: S02 -- Step 1a: Compile source to CDX

  s02-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-cdx = [ScEchoStyled (SeLit "FAIL: CDX compile failed") ClBrightRed True, ScIf (SeFileExists (SeVar "cdxLog")) [ScRaw "Get-Content $cdxLog | Write-Host"] [], ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 1a: Compile source to CDX..."), ScAssign "imgOut" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'disk-test.img'"), ScAssign "cdxOut" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'disk-test.cdx'"), ScAssign "cdxLog" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'cdx-build.log'"), ScRaw "& pwsh -NoProfile -File $compile -Src $SampleSrc -Out $cdxOut -Log $cdxLog -PCore $PCore", ScIf (SeOr (SeRaw "$LASTEXITCODE -ne 0") (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "cdxOut")))) fail-cdx []]

Section: S03 -- Step 1b: CDX to PE via plug

  s03-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-pe = [ScEcho (SeLit "FAIL: PE plug failed"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 1b: CDX -> PE via plug..."), ScAssign "peOut" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'disk-test.efi'"), ScAssign "pePlug" (SeRaw "Join-Path $root 'codex\\plugs\\pe\\run.ps1'"), ScRaw "& pwsh -NoProfile -File $pePlug -CdxInput $cdxOut -Out $peOut", ScIf (SeOr (SeRaw "$LASTEXITCODE -ne 0") (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "peOut")))) fail-pe []]

Section: S04 -- Step 1c: PE + CDX to FAT16 IMG via plug

  s04-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-img = [ScEcho (SeLit "FAIL: IMG plug failed"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 1c: PE + CDX -> FAT16 IMG via plug..."), ScAssign "imgPlug" (SeRaw "Join-Path $root 'codex\\plugs\\img\\run.ps1'"), ScRaw "& pwsh -NoProfile -File $imgPlug -PeInput $peOut -CdxInput $cdxOut -Out $imgOut -Fat16 -Source $SampleSrc", ScIf (SeOr (SeRaw "$LASTEXITCODE -ne 0") (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "imgOut")))) fail-img [], ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  IMG: $((Get-Item $imgOut).Length) bytes\"")]

Section: S05 -- Step 2: Boot compiler with IMG as IDE disk

  s05-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-no-stage0 = [ScEcho (SeRaw "\"FAIL: no compiler CDX at $Stage0\""), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in let fail-vm = [ScEcho (SeLit "FAIL: VM did not start"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 2: DISK compile..."), ScAssign "Stage0" (SeRaw "Join-Path $root 'build-output\\bare-metal\\Codex.cdx'"), ScIf (SeNot (SeFileExists (SeVar "Stage0"))) fail-no-stage0 [], ScRaw "$diskArgs = @('-drive', \"file=$imgOut,format=raw,if=ide,index=0\")", ScRaw "$run = Start-VmRun -Kernel $Stage0 -ConnectTimeoutSec 10 -MemMB 3072 -PCore $PCore -ExtraArgs $diskArgs", ScIf (SeNot (SeVar "run")) fail-vm [], ScBlank]

Section: S05b -- Inside the VM's lifetime

 The try opens only once $run holds a VM. Everything above it can exit, and
 the finally below dereferences $run.Conn, so anything that exits before the
 assignment would die in the cleanup under Set-StrictMode and take its own
 diagnostic with it.

  s05b-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-ready = [ScEcho (SeLit "FAIL: no READY"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScIf (SeNot (SeRaw "(Read-VmReady -Conn $run.Conn -TimeoutSec 30)")) fail-ready []]

Section: S06 -- Send DISK mode commands and read response

  s06-body : List ShellCmd = [ScBlank, ScRaw "$stream = $run.Conn.Data.GetStream()", ScRaw "$hdr = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes(\"DISK`n\")", ScRaw "$stream.Write($hdr, 0, $hdr.Length)", ScRaw "$path = [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8.GetBytes($DiskPath + \"`n\")", ScRaw "$stream.Write($path, 0, $path.Length)", ScRaw "$stream.Flush()", ScAssign "binSize" (SeInt 0), ScAssign "status" (SeLit ""), ScRaw "$logLines = @()"]

Section: S07 -- Read lines until DISK-OUT: or CODEGEN-HALTED

 SIZE: no longer ends the read. In DISK mode it is followed by the write to
 the volume and then DISK-OUT:, which is the line that says the artifact
 exists, so the loop records the size and keeps going.

  s07-body : List ShellCmd =
    let on-size = [ScIf (SeMatch (SeVar "line") "^\\D*(\\d+)") [ScAssign "binSize" (SeRaw "[int]$matches[1]")] [], ScAssign "status" (SeLit "size")]
    in let on-disk-out = [ScAssign "status" (SeLit "disk-out"), ScBreak]
    in let on-halt = [ScAssign "status" (SeLit "error"), ScBreak]
    in let on-errs = [ScAssign "status" (SeLit "error")]
    in [ScBlank, ScLabeledWhile "read_loop" (SeRaw "$true") [ScRaw "$line = Read-StreamLine -Stream $stream -TimeoutSec 120", ScIf (SeRaw "$null -eq $line") [ScBreak] [], ScRaw "$logLines += $line", ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "line") (SeLit "SIZE:")) on-size [], ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "line") (SeLit "DISK-OUT:")) on-disk-out [], ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "line") (SeLit "CODEGEN-HALTED")) on-halt [], ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "line") (SeLit "CODEGEN-ERRORS")) on-errs [], ScIf (SeRaw "$logLines.Count -ge 400") [ScBreak] []]]

Section: S08 -- Validate the compile

  s08-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-compile = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"FAIL: DISK compile failed (status=$status)\"") ClBrightRed True, ScForEach "ll" (SeVar "logLines") [ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  $ll\"")], ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScIf (SeOr (SeStringNeq (SeVar "status") (SeLit "disk-out")) (SeRaw "$binSize -le 0")) fail-compile [], ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Compiled: $binSize bytes\""), ScForEach "ll" (SeVar "logLines") [ScIf (SeStartsWith (SeVar "ll") (SeLit "DISK-OUT:")) [ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  $ll\"")] []]]

Section: S09 -- Cleanup VM

  s09-body : List ShellCmd = [ScRaw "Close-Vm -Conn $run.Conn -Process $run.Process"]

Section: S08b -- Step 2b: Extract OUT.CDX from the image

 Outside the try, because the image is only settled once the VM is closed.
 The guest's declared SIZE: is the oracle for the extraction: a file on the
 volume that disagrees with what the compiler said it wrote is a failure, not
 a rounding.

  s08b-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-size = [ScEchoStyled (SeRaw "\"FAIL: OUT.CDX is $extracted bytes, the guest declared $binSize\"") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 2b: Extract OUT.CDX from the image..."), ScAssign "cdxOut" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'disk-compiled.cdx'"), ScAssign "extracted" (SeRaw "Export-Fat16File -Image $imgOut -Name 'OUT     CDX' -Out $cdxOut"), ScIf (SeRaw "$extracted -ne $binSize") fail-size [], ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Written: $cdxOut ($extracted bytes)\"")]

Section: S10 -- Step 3: Boot compiled CDX and check output

  s10-body : List ShellCmd =
    let fail-run = [ScEcho (SeLit "FAIL: runtime failed"), ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in let pass = [ScEchoStyled (SeLit "PASS: DISK compile mode works") ClBrightGreen True]
    in let fail-mismatch = [ScEchoStyled (SeLit "FAIL: output mismatch") ClBrightRed True, ScExit (SeInt 1)]
    in [ScBlank, ScEcho (SeLit "Step 3: Run compiled CDX..."), ScAssign "actual" (SeRaw "Join-Path $outDir 'runtime.actual'"), ScRaw "& pwsh -NoProfile -File $runScript -Kernel $cdxOut -OutFile $actual -PCore $PCore", ScIf (SeRaw "$LASTEXITCODE -ne 0") fail-run [], ScRaw "$output = if (Test-Path $actual) { (Get-Content -Raw $actual).TrimEnd() } else { '' }", ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Output: '$output'\""), ScEcho (SeRaw "\"  Expected: '$Expected'\""), ScIf (SeStringEq (SeVar "output") (SeVar "Expected")) pass fail-mismatch]

Section: Assembly

  s01 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "preamble", ps-why = "strict mode, the repository root and the paths", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s01-body }

  s01b : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the FAT export helper", ps-why = "defines Export-FatFile, which the later stages call to read a file back off the disk image", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s01b-body }

  s02 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the subject list", ps-why = "names the sources to be compiled from the disk", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "the CDX under test could not be built"], ps-body = s02-body }

  s03 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "build the disk image", ps-why = "writes the subjects into a FAT image, because this harness compiles from the DISK rather than over the wire", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "the PE could not be built from the CDX"], ps-body = s03-body }

  s04 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the guest command line", ps-why = "assembles the codex-vm arguments with the image attached", ps-in = ["Kernel"], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [PrKernel (SeVar "Kernel")], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "the disk image could not be built"], ps-body = s04-body }

  s05 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "boot the guest", ps-why = "starts the guest and refuses when it does not come up, before the exchange below is attempted", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [PrGuests 1], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "stage0 is absent, or the guest did not come up"], ps-body = s05-body }

  s05b : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "open the connection", ps-why = "takes the guest's stream for the exchange", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "the guest never reported ready on its connection"], ps-body = s05b-body }

  s06 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "drive the compiles", ps-why = "asks the guest to compile each subject from the attached disk", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s06-body }

  s07 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "read the results", ps-why = "reads what the guest reported for each subject", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s07-body }

  s08 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "export the artifacts", ps-why = "reads the produced binaries back off the image through Export-FatFile", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "a subject failed to compile from the attached disk"], ps-body = s08-body }

  s09 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "cleanup", ps-why = "closes the guest and its connection HOWEVER the four stages above ended, which is why it is the group's handler", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [], ps-body = s09-body }

  s08b : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "compare the artifacts", ps-why = "runs AFTER the guest is gone, comparing what the disk compile produced against the reference, which is why it is a stage after the group and not inside it", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "an exported artifact disagrees in SIZE with the reference"], ps-body = s08b-body }

  s10 : PipeStage = PipeStage { ps-name = "the verdict", ps-why = "reports the per-subject results and sets the exit code", ps-in = [], ps-out = [], ps-needs = [], ps-verdict = [PoExit 1 "a subject did not run, or its output does not match the reference"], ps-body = s10-body }

  tdc-pipe : Pipeline = Pipeline { pl-name = "test-disk-compile", pl-doc = "Test DISK compile mode end-to-end", pl-params = tdc-params, pl-stages = [PsStage s01, PsStage s01b, PsStage s02, PsStage s03, PsStage s04, PsStage s05, PsGroup None None (Just s09) [PsStage s05b, PsStage s06, PsStage s07, PsStage s08], PsStage s08b, PsStage s10] }

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (emit-powershell (pipeline-to-shell tdc-pipe))
  end

